# Sample CLAUDE.md snippet — wiring in ai-agent-guardrails

Add a section like this to your project's `CLAUDE.md` so Claude (and anyone
reading the repo) knows a guardrail is active, and add the hook config below
to `.claude/settings.json` (project or user scope) so Claude Code actually
invokes it.

## 1. `.claude/settings.json` hook registration

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 /absolute/path/to/ai-agent-guardrails/integrations/claude_code/pretooluse_hook.py"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Adjust the path to wherever you cloned/installed `ai-agent-guardrails`, and
confirm the `hooks` schema against your installed Claude Code version's docs
(`claude --help` / the Claude Code hooks reference) — the hook config shape
has changed across releases, and `pretooluse_hook.py`'s docstring spells out
exactly which parts of the contract this integration assumes.

## 2. CLAUDE.md section

```markdown
## Safety guardrails

This repo has ai-agent-guardrails wired in as a Claude Code PreToolUse hook
(see `.claude/settings.json`). Before any Bash tool call executes, it is
evaluated against the policy set in `ai-agent-guardrails/policies/default.yaml`:

- BLOCK-tier commands (unreviewed `terraform destroy`, `kubectl delete
  namespace`/`--all`, unscoped `rm -rf`, force-push to main/master/production,
  IAM wildcard policy grants, MFA/IAM-identity deletion) are refused before
  they run — Claude will see the block reason and should treat it the same
  as a failed command, not retry around it.
- WARN-tier commands (destructive SQL outside a migration file, `curl | bash`,
  force-push to a non-protected branch) are allowed to proceed but are logged;
  treat a WARN in the transcript as a prompt to double-check the command was
  actually intended.

Every evaluation — allowed, warned, or blocked — is appended to
`~/.guardrails/audit.jsonl` for review.
```

## 3. Sanity-check the wiring

```bash
echo '{"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"terraform destroy"}}' \
  | python3 /absolute/path/to/ai-agent-guardrails/integrations/claude_code/pretooluse_hook.py
# should print a JSON block decision to stdout, a "[guardrails] BLOCKED ..." line to stderr,
# and exit with code 2.
```
